workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the quadratic form \n$Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}.$ \nEvaluate $Q(x)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the expression for $Q(x)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+2\\cdot {1}^{2}+6\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4+2+12 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "18"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1})+{x}_{2}(2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}(-{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(-4){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-4){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "3{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-1){x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+(-1){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}-{x}_{3})+{x}_{2}(3{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}(-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-140928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(3){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(3){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "3{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "3{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+1{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+1{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}+{x}_{3})+{x}_{2}({x}_{2})+{x}_{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & b \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{2}{2}=1\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=1$ and $c=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\nb+c=1-2=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ b & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{(-4)}{2}=-2\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$ and $b=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=2+(-2)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-140932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-140932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & b \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-5){x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}^{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-5){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries ${a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{2}{2}=1,$ and\n\n- we split the coefficient of $-10{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{13}={a}_{31}=\\frac{-10}{2}=-5.$\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,$ $b=-5,$ and $c=3.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=3+(-5)+3=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & b \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}^{2}+(-3){x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-3){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{-6}{2}=-3\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=-3$ and $c=1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\nb+c=-3+1=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & b \\\\ 6 & a & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,6{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}^{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of $12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries ${a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{12}{2}=6,$ and\n\n- we split the coefficient of $-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{13}={a}_{31}=\\frac{-4}{2}=-2.$\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=0.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+0=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99f3570307c15d08fb4264489cfdb2ce62346d9c0518ce443da145d907533d92"} {"question" "q-94120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "q-94120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/state.json" "file_sha256" "47eb17e72a309bc7258c893e6a58dd46ef8ba48be40978e9fbd5fd00f5ae9b11"} {"question" "e-8168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/e51c52e07d49052f578138e5c1d7e9f84a95ba8c454e7fcf834dcc9047dad432.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/example-8168.json" "file_sha256" "2021e61a95c091d801b4c51e2c56297ca5323f269deccfaaa3eb0ecd5b237a93"} {"question" "e-8168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that every quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ has an associated $2 \\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $L$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ since it's a $3 \\times 3$ matrix (not $2 \\times 2$).\n\n- $M$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2.$  Although it's a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, $M$ is not symmetric since $m_{12} \\neq m_{21}.$\n\n- $N$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ since it is a $2 \\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$N$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/example-8168.json" "file_sha256" "2021e61a95c091d801b4c51e2c56297ca5323f269deccfaaa3eb0ecd5b237a93"} {"question" "e-8169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/791b214858b7ff88b6ad1ba98ea8336abbd678ffb34751b041e11cec8cd44143.png)\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$ when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/b7df527ba563debac29dbdd838aadb4f219653a77077b70b65bdbfe579e26a0a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/example-8169.json" "file_sha256" "5e0448d7334a0b2d3e647fff64f569f017070b95096010ff368f8ddef4d7a909"} {"question" "e-8169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/1a8e02bec4af0b88d7fa0f4cd87b9e0f89757ca87f494e1451650ac4f3a06dcf.png) into the expression for $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 23\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =86.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/example-8169.json" "file_sha256" "5e0448d7334a0b2d3e647fff64f569f017070b95096010ff368f8ddef4d7a909"} {"question" "e-8170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/59d795aef27f3ae7598e1a8503ba0dbde377486b355e0db6decc4753f9ae7544.png)\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which expression represents the corresponding quadratic form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$ in terms of the components of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/assets/31a4a301bddfd7435f188f76c1702beb7c2eea01a1b174d5195f321cfdef3103.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14051940/example-8170.json" "file_sha256" "3a4ab3a9d8801d83b3cf04840152dc772b7e6eda5d002cc50a70fc8b25b63922"} {"question" "e-8170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term $a_{ij}x_i x_j$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =-1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(1){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(1){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+-1{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begi